'''Remo''' (Rheno) is an [[extinct language|extinct]] indigenous language once spoken along the [[Môa River]] of [[Amazonas (Peruvian department)|Amazonas]], [[Peru]], one of several [[Panoan languages]] to go by that name.  It was similar to [[Amawaka language|Amawaka]].

